n wanted tommy to  continue on the show in season two  but the actress decided instead to  depart and maggie quietly disappeared  from the cast of characters  tomei however went on to bigger things  four years after leaving a different  world  she won the academy award for best  supporting actress for her hilarious  turn in my cousin vinnie kicking off a  film career that spans three decades  she was nominated for two more oscars  for 2001's in the bedroom  and 2007's the wrestler and has applied  her craft successfully  in both comedies and dramas she returned  to tv in 2007  on the dennis leary led series rescue me  and also had a notable role on empire  she's even worked her way into the  marvel cinematic universe as aunt may to  tom holland's take on spider-man  season one of a different world  acquainted us with whitley gilbert  a snobby hillman student whose stuck-up  attitude was  often played for laughs in contrast to  her more down-to-earth classmates  i mean my dad is a judge and  your daddy's a what a dentist the  character however proved popular and  when bonet left the show  whitley was moved into a central role  her personality was also mellowed and  given added depth  and her opposite to track romance with  the nerdy dwayne wayne  became one of the series central arcs  whitley remained involved with hillman  as a dorm director even after graduating  and ended the series married to dwayne  wayne in carrying the couple's first  child  jasmine guy was awarded multiple naacp  image awards for her portrayal  of whitley this success led guide to a  long and active career as an actor  dancer and choreographer as well as a  director of stage productions  she remained very active on tv showing  up on 90 staples like melrose place and  nypd blue  before landing a lead role on showtime's  dead like me  in the early aughts more recently she  had recurring parts on the vampire  diaries  and disney channel's kc undercover  with his trademark flip up sunglasses  nerdy charisma and rhyming name  dwayne wayne seemed destined for pop  culture residents from his first  appearance on a different world  the characters started out in a  supporting capacity but became central  to the show in season  2 fueled largely by his on-again  off-again romance with whitley  as the years went on he lived in japan  became a math professor  and in the end staged a grand gesture to  win the love of his life  the character was praised in the press  and remains fondly remembered  kadeem hardison's performance as dwayne  wayne made him one of a different  world's breakout stars  and the actor has gone on to a long and  incredibly prolific career in film and  television he's appeared in literally  dozens of movies between 1992 and the  present day  in scores of tv spots including a recent  reunion with jasmine guy  on casey undercover well i don't know to  whom you are referring  drop the phony southern accent you're  not fooling anybody you're not the belle  of this ball  hardison also appeared in the film  paddleton and played a starring role in  the showtime series black monday  as funny as dwayne wayne was he had too  much heart in leading man charm to serve  as a different world's classic fool  fortunately ron johnson was ready and  willing to leap into that archetypal gap  an rotc student and duane's best friend  ron fancies himself a ladies man and is  always up for a get rich quick scheme  he might not have been the most serious  student but he comes out okay  as a manager and co-owner of his own  nightclub despite primarily serving as a  comic role  he did experience his share of drama  coping with a racist incident  and navigating romantic travails with  fellow hillman students kimberly and  freddie  daryl embell who played ron jumped right  back into sitcom work when a different  world ended  booking a lead role on upn's sci-fi  comedy series  homeboys in outer space unfortunately  the show was a critical flop  and was canceled by the network after  one season  bell bounced back with a three-episode  run on the cosby show follow-up  cosby but subsequently moved away from  acting on a regular basis  he remained connected to the industry  however through his friendship with  hardison  who cast spell in his 2013 film the dark  party  he also got a boost from his long-term  relationship with cosby show alum tempus  bledsoe  with whom he'd appear in the 2009  reality show  house husbands of hollywood with whitley  thrust to the fore in a different world  second season  there was a need to expand the cast of  supporting characters  thus we were introduced to kimberly  reese whitley's roommate and eventual  best friend  a biology major she was employed at  campus eatery the pit  and also performed in the banned  expression managed by ron  kimberly was the center of a couple of  the show's more serious arcs  facing a false alarm pregnancy and  choosing to give up a much needed  scholarship  due to the sponsoring corporation's ties  to apartheid era south africa  after graduation she enrolled in medical  school and found love with a fellow  student there  kimberly was portrayed by charnell brown  who came to a different world from a  broadway stage career  after the show ended she did spot work  on tv showing up in episodes of martin  and living single  she also worked as a singer and a  fashion designer and the past decade has  seen her enter the world of film  production  she returned to the front of the camera  in 2020 with an appearance in an episode  of fifth ward  most of the hillman students on a  different world were your typical  college kids  except for jaleesa vincent taylor i'm  denise you must be 26.  oh i didn't mean that you don't look 26  you know you don't even look a day over  why don't we just  start over at 25 having enrolled after a  failed marriage  she brought a level of maturity to the  proceedings that provided a contrast  with some of her more fresh-faced  classmates  a business management major she worked  part-time at the hillman library  and as the assistant dorm director of  gilbert hall  one of her central plot lines saw her in  a relationship with coach walter oakes  but that would end with the two calling  things off at the altar  jaleesa wound up starting her own temp  agency and marrying colonel bradford  taylor  jalisa was played by dawn lewis who  brought more to the show than her acting  chops  an accomplished singer she also co-wrote  the show's theme song  a feat she would repeat with a little  help from r b group in vogue for her  next gig  hanging with mr cooper her resume is  stuffed with roles in films like dream  girls  and a metric ton of television work in  particular  lewis found a lucrative avenue in voice  work lending her talents to everything  from futurama and the boondocks  to rick and morty and the simpsons most  recently  you might have caught her in a pair of  reboots as marsha langdon on the 2019  return of veronica mars  and as the voice of the chief in  netflix's animated take on carmen san  diego  for many young people the college years  are about social consciousness and  political activism  such was the case with freddie brooks  who arrived in the season 2 premiere as  jalisa's roommate  a free spirit whose mother was a 60s  hippie freddie became a student activist  during her time at hillman  advocating for a number of different  environmental community and charitable  causes  that's not to say she didn't have time  for personal matters though  as she spent her early time at school  pining after dwayne wayne  only to eventually end up in a  relationship with ron  freddy ended the series completing her  first year in law school  cree summer who played freddie didn't go  on to the most successful live-action  career  appearing in only a handful of films and  tv shows per decade  her voice acting resume however is  straight up staggering  she was already established in the  business prior to a different world  having originated the voice of penny on  inspector gadget  after the series wrapped up she  continued down that avenue  contributing her vocal talents to all  kinds of classic shows captain planet  gargoyles superman the animated series  kim possible  star wars the clone wars and rugrats  just to name a few  frankly if you have enjoyed animation at  all in the last couple of decades  you have enjoyed summer's work she's one  of the most important and influential  voice actors of the modern era  introduced in season two lieutenant  colonel bradford taylor started out as a  recurring character  but eventually moved up to become part  of the main cast  a career military man and veteran of the  vietnam war  he had previously served in the same  unit as pit proprietor vernon gaines  and remained martially minded enough  that the students nicknamed him dr war  some people like to call him dr who are  people who major in indoor outdoor  breathing  everybody calls him dr ward aka student  enemy number one  at hillman he headed up the rotc unit  that included ron johnson  and worked as a professor of mathematics  which led to him crossing paths with  dwayne wayne  eventually he ended up marrying and  fathering a child with jaleesa vincent  taylor  colonel taylor was played by glenn  turman who had already been acting in  film and tv for over 25  years before arriving on a different  world he remained very active after the  show wrapped  if you've watched tv or seen a movie in  the past 30 years  you've likely caught one of his  performances notable recent efforts  include the wire  in which he played baltimore mayor  clarence royce jj abrams 2011 film super  8  shonda rhimes thriller series how to get  away with murder and the stephen king  adaptation mr mercedes  not many people at the college level  could manage coaching the football  basketball baseball and track programs  but then  not many people are walter oaks this  colorful character was another recurring  personality